Enumeration is a crictical part of cybersecurity. It is finding all of the routes to attack a target.
Functions and/or resources that allow us to interact with the target and/or provide additional information.
Information that provides us with even more important information to access our target.
Manual enumeration is a critical component.
Network Mapper (Nmap) is an open-source network analysis and security auditing tool written in C, C++, Python, and Lua.
Nmap scans networks and highlights key information regarding the target.
Nmap offers scans such as host discovery, port scanning, and os detection.
Nmap syntax is similar as I have done but with nmap in front like this  hellopandagas@htb[/htb]$ nmap <scan types> <options> <target>.
nmap --help displays scanning techniques
Scanning Options	Description
  10.129.2.0/24	Target network range.
  -sn	Disables port scanning.
  -oA tnet	Stores the results in all formats starting with the name 'tnet'.
